{"name":"Romantic","hex":"#ffc69e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Romantic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to Romance.","Of or pertaining to Romanticism."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An artist involved in the Romantic movement."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Romantic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Romanticism","blocks":[{"text":"Romanticism was an artistic and intellectual movement that originated in Europe towards the end of the 18th century. The purpose of the movement was to advocate for the importance of subjectivity, imagination, and appreciation of nature in society and culture in response to the Age of Enlightenment and the Industrial Revolution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Caspar_David_Friedrich_-_Wanderer_above_the_Sea_of_Fog.jpeg/330px-Caspar_David_Friedrich_-_Wanderer_above_the_Sea_of_Fog.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romanticism","wikidata":"Q37068"},{"title":"Romantic music","blocks":[{"text":"Romantic music is a stylistic movement in Western Classical music associated with the period of the 19th century commonly referred to as the Romantic era. It is closely related to the broader concept of Romanticism—the intellectual, artistic, and literary movement that became prominent in Western culture from about 1798 until 1837."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Danhauser%2C_Josef_-_Franz_Liszt_am_Fl%C3%BCgel_phantasierend.jpg/330px-Danhauser%2C_Josef_-_Franz_Liszt_am_Fl%C3%BCgel_phantasierend.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romantic_music","wikidata":"Q207591"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Delacroix_-_La_Mort_de_Sardanapale_%281827%29.jpg/500px-Delacroix_-_La_Mort_de_Sardanapale_%281827%29.jpg?utm_sour